Apple plans to announce its earnings for the fourth fiscal quarter of 2026 on Monday, November 2, according to the company's <a href="https://investor.apple.com/investor-relations/default.aspx">updated Investor Relations page</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-834994" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2022/01/Apple-Logo-Cash-Feature-Yellow.jpg" alt="" width="2676" height="1504" /><br/>
The earnings report will be available at 1:30 p.m. Pacific Time on November 2, with new Apple CEO John Ternus and CFO Kevan Parekh to discuss the results during a 2:00 p.m. Pacific Time phone call. Apple will stream the call on its website.<br/>
<br/>
Apple's Q4 2026 earnings will cover launch-week <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> sales. Apple also released the Apple Watch Series 12, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-watch-ultra/">Apple Watch Ultra 4</a>, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/airpods/">AirPods 5</a> during the quarter. The <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> won't be included because the quarter covers the period between June 28 and September 26, and the device won't launch until October 23.<br/>
<br/>
Apple executives could comment on memory pricing and supply constraints, as well as share holiday quarter expectations.<br/>
<br/>
During Apple's Q3 2026 call, Parekh said total company revenue would grow 9 to 11 percent year-over-year in the September quarter. Apple expects iPhone revenue to be affected by foreign exchange headwinds and supply constraints, with growth in the mid-teens year-over-year.<br/>
<br/>
